# Amendment #33 — primary-persona memory-consumer wiring (D7)

2026-04-23. Delivers the D7 memory-consumer wiring per amendment
plan `docs/rebuild/plans/amendment-33-memory-consumer-wiring-
primary-persona.md` + research doc `docs/rebuild/plans/research/
amendment-33-memory-consumer-wiring-research.md`. D7's sibling D8
(session-start context-load gate) shipped at amendment #32 and
landed the shared `ComposedContextPayload` composer + contributor
registry; D7 REGISTERS a turn-level memory-retrieval contributor
against that existing registry (plan §3 constraint 3).

The amendment lands one new module inside the primary-persona
fence:

  - `primary-persona/src/memory_consumer.py` — the D7 wiring:
    - `MemoryClient` Protocol bound against amendment #24's MCP
      tool surface (`add_episode`, `search`). Persona never
      imports memory-system source.
    - `resolve_workspace_slug(workspace_root)` — pure-function
      basename sanitisation matching
      `workspace_bootstrap.adapters.first_run_scaffold.
      workspace_slug`. Parity-tested against the canonical on a
      fixture set (AC-D7.4). Precedent: hands-off-lifecycle ships
      the same pattern with the same parity discipline.
    - `TurnAggregator` + `close_turn(...)` — per-turn
      aggregation; exactly one `add_episode` per user↔AI turn;
      fire-and-forget via `asyncio.create_task` (AC-D7.2,
      AC-D7.3). Structurally non-blocking per plan §3
      constraint 5.
    - `build_memory_retrieval_contributor` +
      `register_memory_retrieval` — factory + registration
      helper for the turn-level contributor. Issues one `search`
      per `UserPromptSubmit` with `group_ids=[workspace_slug]`
      (AC-D7.4), returns a plain-text block under a soft
      character cap (AC-D7.6). Fail-closed on every memory-
      boundary exception (AC-D7.7).

No source edits outside `primary-persona/src/`. No edits to
`context_composer.py`, `session_start_gate.py`, or any other
existing primary-persona module — the D7 surface is purely
additive.

AC surface (AC-D7.1 – AC-D7.7 + AC-D7.S) — 16 tests covering 7
outcome-shaped criteria:

  - AC-D7.1: turn-start retrieval lands in `UserPromptSubmit`
    additionalContext; the search call carries the workspace
    slug in `group_ids`.
  - AC-D7.2: exactly one aggregated episode per user↔AI turn
    (not per-message, not per-state-event); single-turn fixture
    produces 1 call; three-turn fixture produces 3 calls; body
    captures both the user message and the persona reply.
  - AC-D7.3: interactive turn returns promptly while a prior
    write is held on an `asyncio.Event` (stand-in for the 113 s
    empirical per-episode cost); next-turn `on_user_prompt_submit`
    completes in well under 1 s.
  - AC-D7.4: every search's `group_ids` and every add_episode's
    `group_id` equals the workspace slug; parity test against
    canonical `workspace_bootstrap.workspace_slug` on six
    fixture basenames; unrepresentable basename raises a
    structural `WorkspaceSlugUnrepresentableError`.
  - AC-D7.5: session-level + turn-level contributors co-exist
    on the shared registry; session entry-point fires only
    session contributors; turn entry-point fires only turn
    contributors; late-binding of the turn contributor after
    session composition still picks up on turn-fire (registry
    is the authority, not any cached state).
  - AC-D7.6: memory-retrieval contribution respects its soft
    char cap; combined awareness-sized + memory-retrieval
    contributions pass through the composer's structural 10 000-
    char refusal (the D8-owned Pydantic `_cap_guard`).
  - AC-D7.7: every boundary failure class (connection refused,
    HTTP 5xx, asyncio.TimeoutError, OSError) yields an empty
    memory-retrieval contribution and the turn proceeds; the
    awareness-block path is unaffected.
  - AC-D7.S: seal-diff discipline — only primary-persona/ +
    plans/ + universal paths changed (verified by
    `test_no_sealed_amendments.py` which amendment #32
    established).

Method-level choices (builder's call per ODD §1.1, plan §3
constraint 10):

  - Async shape: `asyncio.create_task` fire-and-forget. The
    research §3.3.1 lean (background-scope via orchestrator)
    would require a new scope-kind; research §3.3.2
    (orchestrator-internal task) would require an orchestrator
    amendment. Both blocked by plan §3 constraint 2 (no
    cross-component source edits). `asyncio.create_task` is
    the cheapest non-amendment shape that satisfies plan §3
    constraint 5 (structurally non-blocking).
  - Query shape: raw user prompt (research §4.2 #1). Research
    leans toward #2 (prompt + last-3-turn context), but that
    requires a persona-layer conversation-history primitive
    this amendment does not ship (would expand scope).
    Candidate-2 is non-blocked future work; AC-D7.1 measures
    retrieval happens, not the query shape.
  - Retention class: default-normal (research §5.2). Memory-
    system's D10 tagger enforces it; the persona-override path
    is non-blocked future work once persona-layer has content
    classification primitives.
  - Retrieval payload soft cap: 1600 chars (upper-band of
    research §4.3's 200–400 token budget).
  - `center_node_uuid`: `None` at v1. Persona-layer does not
    yet carry an active-scope primary-entity primitive;
    wiring it is non-blocked future work once scope-of-work
    exposes an anchor-entity surface the persona can read.

Out of scope (plan §8):

  - Other candidate consumers (scope-of-work, orchestrator,
    objective-tracker, self-correction) — deferred per research
    §10.
  - Per-scope `group_id` — v1 is per-workspace only (Rule B).
  - Session-close / per-message aggregation — ruled out
    (Rules C + research §3.1).
  - D8's session-level contributor — shipped at amendment #32.
  - Memory-system source amendments — MCP surface consumed
    as-is (amendment #24).
  - Orchestrator / scope-of-work source amendments — the
    research §3.3.1 / §3.3.2 leans both require an amendment
    the plan §3 constraint 2 fence rules out; `asyncio.create_
    task` is the non-amendment shape selected.
  - Cost-governance source amendments (plan §9 halt #8) —
    `asyncio.create_task` has no triggering-scope budget
    attribution; neither research §3.2 candidate requires
    cost-governance source changes.
  - New OTel spans beyond the persona layer's existing D9
    surface.
  - Workspace-supplied persona content (`prompt.md` /
    `contract.yaml`) — workspace-owned.

